WEBVTT

00:03.420 --> 00:05.500
About a hundred years ago.

00:06.300 --> 00:10.440
This? Why this is the story of a little girl,

00:10.480 --> 00:13.020
who travelled beyond the Door of Destiny.

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
NAAJA

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
Nadja,

00:18.000 --> 00:20.540
With your eyes

00:18.000 --> 00:20.540
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
Nadja,

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
NAAJA

00:21.750 --> 00:24.010
What do you see?

00:21.750 --> 00:24.010
Nani ga mieru

00:24.210 --> 00:27.090
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.210 --> 00:27.090
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.220 --> 00:29.430
The door to the future,

00:27.220 --> 00:29.430
Mirai no tobira

00:30.320 --> 00:33.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:30.320 --> 00:33.560
Sagashite iru

00:34.280 --> 00:41.580
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:34.280 --> 00:41.580
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:45.420
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:41.660 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:52.130
It could be so much more fun

00:48.920 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:55.630
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.210 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:59.350
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.050 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.440 --> 01:08.560
I will go waving

01:06.440 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:15.490
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:08.860 --> 01:15.490
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:18.200
But I won't look back

01:15.490 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:23.410
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.450 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:27.080
Nadja, Your smile

01:23.660 --> 01:27.080
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:30.420
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.080 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:33.550
Under the blue sky,

01:30.630 --> 01:33.550
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:36.380
I will find the place

01:33.550 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:40.600
where my future lies

01:36.970 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

02:43.080 --> 02:44.960
Thanks, thanks!

02:45.300 --> 02:45.920
Ready?

02:46.000 --> 02:47.980
Relax and pretend it's just practice.

02:50.620 --> 02:51.960
Do your best, Nadja!

02:52.820 --> 02:54.580
Now, the one you've all been waiting for...

02:55.000 --> 02:57.400
The miraculous dancing princess who descended from heaven, Nadja!

03:11.200 --> 03:15.120
Dancing Princess Nadja and the Mummy Professor

03:29.120 --> 03:31.920
What do you think? She's so daring.

03:39.020 --> 03:39.840
Alright!

03:47.640 --> 03:49.840
That girl really is great.

03:49.940 --> 03:53.580
She makes all my hard work worthwhile.

03:57.040 --> 03:57.680
Now!

04:26.340 --> 04:27.760
Hello Christian.

04:29.800 --> 04:31.440
Ah... Director.

04:33.780 --> 04:35.400
I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

04:35.620 --> 04:37.680
Oh, no, no. Don't worry about me.

04:37.740 --> 04:39.580
More importantly, I'm glad that the books are all right.

04:39.740 --> 04:42.420
As you know, all the books here are rare and priceless.

04:42.900 --> 04:44.200
I'm very sorry.

04:45.800 --> 04:48.240
Putting that aside, you sure are working hard every day.

04:48.500 --> 04:51.220
Oh, and how is your research going?

04:51.740 --> 04:52.920
It's getting there.

04:53.420 --> 04:56.200
Egyptology is a deep subject.

04:56.540 --> 04:59.460
Professor Harrison found a good student in you.

04:59.820 --> 05:03.260
I can only imagine how proud he would be if he was still alive.

05:03.780 --> 05:05.240
Thank you very much.

05:06.820 --> 05:08.020
Professor Harrison...

05:11.380 --> 05:13.260
Oh? You're here again today?

05:13.680 --> 05:15.400
You seem to be really interested...

05:15.820 --> 05:17.720
But, what about your school?

05:18.320 --> 05:19.540
School is...

05:23.520 --> 05:24.180
I see.

05:24.940 --> 05:28.620
Anyway, you come to look at those scarabs everyday... why is that?

05:29.260 --> 05:31.680
I... want to be an Egyptologist!

05:32.160 --> 05:32.920
Oh...

05:33.720 --> 05:36.760
Then the professor put me through school...

05:37.400 --> 05:39.300
...and even allowed me to help with his research.

05:41.260 --> 05:42.040
I know that someday...

05:42.360 --> 05:43.560
I'll go to Egypt, and...

05:43.920 --> 05:46.140
...dig up history with my own hands!

05:53.460 --> 05:54.480
This is awesome!

05:54.920 --> 05:57.380
It's been a while since we've had it this full, huh?

06:00.120 --> 06:01.200
What is it, Rita?

06:01.360 --> 06:04.280
You're trying to say that it's because Nadja's dancing was superb, right?

06:05.600 --> 06:07.060
Thank you, Rita!

06:08.800 --> 06:11.660
When you pulled off your skirt and quickly changed your costume,

06:11.680 --> 06:13.340
the audience went gasping for air!

06:13.760 --> 06:16.080
As expected, Granny's ideas are the best.

06:16.340 --> 06:17.080
Yep.

06:17.400 --> 06:20.140
But more than anything, it's all thanks to the dancing.

06:20.520 --> 06:22.460
Thank you Granny, everyone.

06:22.700 --> 06:25.920
I think so many patrons turned up because I drove the mechanical car around...

06:26.100 --> 06:27.940
Waaaah! Out of the way!!

06:28.640 --> 06:31.920
...and the newspapers reported it, right?

06:32.060 --> 06:34.040
Yeah, after you stole it!

06:34.340 --> 06:37.540
I told you I didn't steal it!! It started running before I knew anything...!

06:38.360 --> 06:41.940
Anyway, my samurai show was pretty popular too!

06:43.960 --> 06:45.800
Right, right, Rita?

06:45.960 --> 06:49.020
You're the only one who understands me!

06:50.680 --> 06:52.640
All right! At any rate, everyone did a great job.

06:53.080 --> 06:54.920
We'll take a break until the afternoon performance.

06:55.680 --> 06:59.020
Yay! I want to go see the inside of that museum!

06:59.400 --> 07:00.400
Kennosuke...

07:00.620 --> 07:02.940
W-What? Did I say something bad?

07:03.560 --> 07:05.840
I hope you're not going to cause trouble again.

07:05.980 --> 07:06.840
No way...

07:08.140 --> 07:09.980
Well then, let's all watch over Kennosuke...

07:10.320 --> 07:11.780
Shall we all go to the museum?

07:12.640 --> 07:13.740
Sounds like fun!

07:13.820 --> 07:14.610
Let's go! Let's go!

07:15.260 --> 07:17.080
Should have kept my mouth shut...

07:18.560 --> 07:22.400
Well then, I guess I'll get some work done while you're gone.

07:23.920 --> 07:26.580
There is a real Japanese katana here!

07:28.040 --> 07:28.640
Let's go!

07:28.740 --> 07:31.200
Hey, hey, let's not cause a scene now.

07:33.220 --> 07:34.360
There goes trouble.

07:34.440 --> 07:35.380
Hello!

07:35.820 --> 07:37.540
George Haskell!

07:37.660 --> 07:39.360
Director! It's been a while!

07:39.580 --> 07:41.540
I'm happy to see you looking well, as usual.

07:41.560 --> 07:42.700
You too, Director.

07:42.760 --> 07:46.320
So I heard you've scored a huge hit again with your recent performance?

07:46.520 --> 07:47.380
It was nothing.

07:47.540 --> 07:50.700
By the way, I got something interesting again.

07:51.040 --> 07:51.960
Oh?

07:52.880 --> 07:54.660
Master and the Director are...?

07:55.000 --> 07:57.340
Those two are very old friends.

07:57.520 --> 07:58.300
Really?

07:58.460 --> 08:00.140
It sounds intriguing.

08:00.520 --> 08:03.380
When those two meet, trouble always happens.

08:04.100 --> 08:05.480
We can only pray...

08:06.160 --> 08:07.360
...that it doesn't happen this time.

08:07.580 --> 08:08.060
Geez.

08:09.660 --> 08:12.260
Don't those two kids know how to behave?

08:12.340 --> 08:13.340
Let's go.

08:31.800 --> 08:33.260
Wow!

08:39.460 --> 08:40.960
A m-mummuy?!

08:42.960 --> 08:44.860
Oh... Wow!

08:48.580 --> 08:50.200
Oh! How cute!

08:54.580 --> 08:57.640
I wonder if these are the toys of an Egyptian prince of princess?

08:57.900 --> 08:58.520
Not at all.

08:59.480 --> 09:01.020
These are not toys.

09:01.540 --> 09:07.380
Molded in the shape of the god Horus' four sons Imsety, Hapy, Duamutef and Qebehsenuef,

09:07.680 --> 09:08.640
these are canopic jars.

09:09.080 --> 09:10.300
Canopic jars...?

09:10.540 --> 09:13.660
Containers used to store the organs which are removed during mummification.

09:14.920 --> 09:16.180
Mummy's organs!?

09:17.440 --> 09:18.360
I'm sorry!

09:18.480 --> 09:20.200
N-No, it's all right.

09:22.360 --> 09:23.080
Cute...

09:25.920 --> 09:26.820
Oh my.

09:27.360 --> 09:28.480
A-Ah! Let me...

09:28.820 --> 09:31.360
Aah! Uh, t-t-thank you...

09:31.620 --> 09:33.540
A-Ancient Egyptians believed that,

09:33.600 --> 09:37.120
their spirits will return to their bodies once in a while even after they're dead.

09:37.760 --> 09:41.200
For that, their bodies have to remain in their complete form.

09:41.720 --> 09:44.800
That's why they tried to preserve their bodies with mummification.

09:45.100 --> 09:47.720
But if you leave organs inside, the human body decays easily.

09:47.920 --> 09:50.740
T-That's why the liver, lungs, stomach and intestines

09:50.940 --> 09:53.660
were placed in these god-shaped canopic jars...

09:53.940 --> 09:55.220
To protect them.

09:58.260 --> 10:00.960
But maybe girls... aren't interested in hearing this type of stuff, huh...?

10:01.460 --> 10:04.780
No, not at all. I couldn't understand the diffuicult parts, but...

10:05.320 --> 10:08.660
The Egyptians must have felt really sad when a family member died as well...

10:09.220 --> 10:11.020
...and wished that they would come back to life...

10:11.060 --> 10:12.720
At least, that's what I imagine...

10:12.860 --> 10:14.280
Oh... You are...

10:14.120 --> 10:15.100
Nadja!

10:15.500 --> 10:16.980
Nadja, where are you?

10:16.240 --> 10:17.560
Everyone's looking for me.

10:18.180 --> 10:18.880
See you!

10:19.300 --> 10:20.240
Nadja?

10:30.000 --> 10:32.900
Geez, where has that Nadja hidden herself?

10:33.340 --> 10:33.880
Damn...

10:34.820 --> 10:37.500
If she hides herself in a crowded place like this...

10:37.660 --> 10:38.980
...we'll never find her!

10:39.280 --> 10:41.700
W-W-Wha? Uh?

10:42.620 --> 10:45.680
Boss! Wait for me!

10:48.660 --> 10:49.860
Boss!

11:41.840 --> 11:42.700
Nadja...?

12:21.000 --> 12:22.780
Miss Edna, good morning.

12:23.940 --> 12:25.320
Oh my, good morning, Christian.

12:26.580 --> 12:29.560
My, you're in extra high spirits today.

12:29.660 --> 12:31.620
Did something good happen?

12:31.640 --> 12:33.200
No, it's nothing.

12:35.900 --> 12:37.080
Here, get ready, Rita.

12:39.900 --> 12:40.460
Here.

12:40.640 --> 12:41.160
Yup!

12:43.240 --> 12:46.240
This is the interesting thing I mentioned yesterday.

12:46.680 --> 12:47.600
Oh?

12:48.220 --> 12:49.120
What do you think?

12:49.840 --> 12:50.980
This is...!

13:01.240 --> 13:01.840
Here!

13:02.620 --> 13:03.560
Here, Nadja!

13:04.020 --> 13:04.660
Aah!

13:05.380 --> 13:06.260
Ah, wait!

13:08.580 --> 13:10.300
W-What, what?

13:10.780 --> 13:13.540
Aah! I'm so sorry! Are you all right?

13:13.720 --> 13:14.820
Y-Yeah...

13:17.240 --> 13:18.300
Ah, you're...?

13:19.340 --> 13:20.780
Mr. Mummy Professor!

13:21.040 --> 13:22.060
Mummy Professor?

13:22.620 --> 13:24.520
What are you doing so early in the morning?

13:25.820 --> 13:28.320
I came to borrow a book I'm using for today's class,

13:28.620 --> 13:30.040
but I came a bit too early, I guess.

13:30.360 --> 13:30.980
I see.

13:31.480 --> 13:32.420
Rita!

13:36.020 --> 13:36.880
Who is that, you ask?

13:37.280 --> 13:38.720
How would I know?

13:38.920 --> 13:39.740
Come on, hurry.

13:40.560 --> 13:42.940
But calling me "Mummy Professor" is mean.

13:43.100 --> 13:45.620
But that's because... you know so much about mummies!

13:45.940 --> 13:48.800
I'm Christian, Christian Strand. Nice to meet you.

13:49.040 --> 13:50.140
I'm Nadja.

13:50.440 --> 13:53.020
I'm a dancer in the Dandelion Troupe.

13:53.280 --> 13:54.980
The miraculous dancing princess, Nadja.

13:55.120 --> 13:55.760
Hmm?

14:15.740 --> 14:17.020
So beautiful...

14:17.860 --> 14:21.120
I'm sure Nefertiti of the Amarna period must have been like you...

14:21.720 --> 14:23.480
Nefer...titi?

14:23.840 --> 14:27.280
The name Nefertiti means, "the beautiful woman has come."

14:28.300 --> 14:31.460
The queen of Akhenaten, a king during Egypt's 18th dynasty.

14:32.100 --> 14:35.240
Those two were said to be the most loving of husbands and wives.

14:36.640 --> 14:40.100
But, the two are still burried somewhere in the desert.

14:41.160 --> 14:42.460
In Egypt's desert?

14:55.120 --> 14:57.440
I wonder if those two listened to the songs of birds,

14:57.840 --> 15:00.080
or gazed at beautiful flowers, too?

15:00.580 --> 15:01.440
This is the first time...

15:01.840 --> 15:05.580
any girl has listed to me with interest like you have.

15:05.820 --> 15:06.340
Eh?

15:07.120 --> 15:08.360
U-Uh, as for me...

15:08.660 --> 15:11.460
Some day, I want to go to Egypt and find their tombs.

15:11.900 --> 15:13.140
That's great!

15:14.460 --> 15:15.080
Here!

15:16.200 --> 15:17.700
Who the heck is that guy?

15:19.040 --> 15:21.800
Oh yeah, I have to go to the university now,

15:22.140 --> 15:27.560
but after classes are over, I'll bring you a book which has a portrait thought to be of Nefertiti.

15:27.600 --> 15:29.020
Ahh! I'd like that!

15:34.140 --> 15:35.700
Hey, everyone!

15:34.940 --> 15:35.680
W-What?

15:36.260 --> 15:38.940
Change of plans. Today's performance is cancelled.

15:39.280 --> 15:41.700
We're off to the great continent of Europe!

15:42.760 --> 15:44.320
But we just got changed!!

15:44.780 --> 15:46.700
His bad habit has appeared again.

15:47.060 --> 15:48.620
Don't tell me we're going treasure hunting again?

15:48.720 --> 15:49.420
That's absolutely right.

15:49.900 --> 15:54.780
I got my hands on a treasure map from the director! It's unmistakably genuine this time!

15:55.020 --> 15:56.360
Sounds fishy to me.

15:56.640 --> 15:59.740
I bet this will turn into a wild goose chase as usual...

16:00.300 --> 16:03.380
I know what you guys are saying! BUT!

16:03.900 --> 16:06.140
When I say we're setting off, WE'RE SETTING OFF!

16:08.220 --> 16:10.580
The Master's crazy about treasure hunting.

16:10.880 --> 16:11.600
I see...

16:11.880 --> 16:12.840
I understand.

16:13.240 --> 16:17.220
But before we cross to the continent, I have somewhere we have to go first.

16:17.560 --> 16:18.120
Huh?

16:21.980 --> 16:23.900
All right, all right.

16:49.400 --> 16:51.300
The report is due the day after tomorrow.

17:18.360 --> 17:19.060
Why?

17:19.440 --> 17:20.340
Christian.

17:21.140 --> 17:22.960
This is a letter from Nadja.

17:25.480 --> 17:26.060
"I'm sorry."

17:26.800 --> 17:29.360
"We suddenly had to set off."

17:30.260 --> 17:34.440
"But I look forward to you showing me Nefertiti's picture someday."

17:35.040 --> 17:35.680
"Nadja."

17:37.500 --> 17:39.520
I met my wife...

17:39.760 --> 17:42.480
...when I was around your age.

18:31.600 --> 18:32.720
Well, that should do it.

18:32.740 --> 18:34.000
Wow, it's great!

18:34.340 --> 18:37.200
Granny, you really can make anything!

18:38.460 --> 18:39.360
Let me see, let me see!

18:40.640 --> 18:41.680
What do you think, everyone?

18:41.700 --> 18:42.560
Hey, Granny.

18:42.880 --> 18:44.800
Where is this place that you have to stop by first?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.300
The Duke of Harcourt's mansion.

18:47.740 --> 18:51.820
The Duke's younger sister, Lady Queensbury, is one of my best customers.

18:52.220 --> 18:55.560
So you were making this hat for her?

18:55.900 --> 18:59.800
The one for spring that she ordered the last time we came to London.

18:59.980 --> 19:04.720
But, why is Lady Queensbury always at the Duke's mansion.

19:05.020 --> 19:10.140
Duke Harcourt's wife died while her sone was still young...

19:10.260 --> 19:13.860
So his younger sister Miss Emma, that is Lady Queensbury,

19:14.140 --> 19:18.580
looks after him like a mother and visits him every so often, even after she got married.

19:18.840 --> 19:19.920
I see...

19:21.180 --> 19:22.720
He doesn't have a mother...

19:22.840 --> 19:24.800
The son of the Duke...

19:24.940 --> 19:28.320
....must feel lonely like I do.

19:29.320 --> 19:32.300
We should be able to see Duke Harcout's mansion soon.

19:32.740 --> 19:33.880
Eh? Really?

19:35.720 --> 19:38.100
The English nobles of this era,

19:38.280 --> 19:43.480
owned large estates away from the city, where they built huge mansions.

19:45.000 --> 19:47.000
Wow, what a huge house!

19:47.140 --> 19:48.260
It's not just the house.

19:48.560 --> 19:51.780
The forest and the lake in this area are all property of the Duke.

19:52.060 --> 19:52.760
Eh?!

19:52.840 --> 19:54.040
Wow!

20:28.360 --> 20:30.060
Thank you for coming.

20:30.420 --> 20:32.460
You're looking lovely today.

20:41.560 --> 20:42.500
Over here!

20:42.720 --> 20:44.400
My, if it isn't Granny!

20:44.500 --> 20:45.900
It's been a while!

20:45.980 --> 20:50.520
I've brought the spring hat that Lady Emma ordered.

20:51.040 --> 20:54.060
They're having a party today, so everyone's busy.

20:54.180 --> 20:55.860
Ah! Should I come back another time?

20:55.920 --> 20:59.840
Not at all, if she hears that you left, Lady Emma would be so disappointed.

21:35.260 --> 21:37.040
It's... all right now.

21:51.840 --> 21:53.640
The star-eyed... knight...

22:14.490 --> 22:17.740
Paris is sunnier than London

22:14.490 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:27.540
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:21.370 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
Indeed

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
It's not use worrying about it

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:38.630
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:35.500 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:43.600
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:38.890 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
To be, to be

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:50.400
The tree fog won

22:45.390 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:54.780
The world frog-jumping contest

22:50.860 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:04.160
Under the kitten's paw

22:57.990 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:10.750
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:04.580 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:16.920
Paris is sunnier than London

23:13.590 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:26.890
It's not the time to hang around

23:20.510 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:32.270
Indeed, indeed

23:27.770 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:40.540 --> 23:41.840
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:41.860 --> 23:44.220
Wow, so this is a ball?

23:44.780 --> 23:46.440
What a splendid world!

23:47.100 --> 23:48.520
I can't believe it.

23:48.740 --> 23:52.000
It's a different world from the one I live in.

23:52.620 --> 23:55.110
Hey, I can hear the rhythm of a waltz.

23:55.740 --> 23:57.080
I want to dance, right now, too!

23:57.900 --> 23:59.460
Eh? You're...

24:00.260 --> 24:01.940
The star-eyed knight...?

24:02.720 --> 24:06.030
The Starry Night, A Waltz Just For the Two

24:02.720 --> 24:03.520
Tomorrow's Nadja:

24:03.920 --> 24:05.910
The Starry Night, A Waltz Just For the Two

24:06.740 --> 24:08.420
Now the Door of Destiny opens.
